    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0148" n="122" xml:id="pg122"/>

                <head>47. National Security Action Memorandum No. 81<anchor n="0" xml:id="d47-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-08-28">August 28,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>Secretary of the Treasury</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>U.S. Gold Position</item>
                </list>
                <p>I would like to have as soon as the Treasury has made an analysis an up-to-date
                    study of our gold position. How much we are losing. How this compares to other
                    years. Whether we can look for a better result in the next six months. What
                    should we do about it.</p>
                <p>I gathered the other day that one of the reasons for the flow of gold was the
                    investment by Americans of dollars in Western Europe. Should I before Congress
                    leaves announce that we are going to put this on a must basis of legislation
                    next year that will make it retroactive to September 1st of this year. Would
                    that help discourage a flow in the next four months?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John F. Kennedy</hi><anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d47-f2"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
